<figure class="cache-figure" data-atomic-fill>
 <p class="figure-title">The atomic boundary surrounds Redis, not the source database</p>
 <label class="cache-field">Order of events <select data-mode aria-label="Source change order"><option value="before">Invalidate before the fill script</option><option value="after">Commit source change after the fill script</option></select></label>
 <div class="atomic-source"><small>Source database · independent commit</small><strong data-source>£12</strong></div>
 <div class="atomic-boundary"><span class="atomic-boundary-label">Redis atomic operation boundary</span><div class="cache-copy-pair"><div class="cache-copy"><small>Current generation</small><strong data-generation>g1</strong></div><div class="cache-copy"><small>Cached card</small><strong data-cache>empty</strong></div></div><p class="atomic-check">Compare expected <b>g1</b> → if equal, save <b>£12</b> with TTL</p><p data-script></p></div>
 <div class="cache-controls"><button data-back>Previous event</button><button data-next>Next event</button><button data-reset>Reset fill</button></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>The complete script is one Redis operation. Generation change and deletion are also one Redis operation in this model. The source commit and delivery of invalidation are separate events; an atomic script cannot eliminate that gap.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {guardFrame} from '../../lib/caching/atomicity.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-atomic-fill]').forEach(root=>{let step=0;const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]')!;const render=()=>{const s=guardFrame(select.value,step);for(const k of['source','generation','cache','script','explanation'])root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=k==='source'?`£${s.source}`:k==='explanation'?s.message:s[k];root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!.disabled=step===0;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!.disabled=step===3;};select.onchange=()=>{step=0;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!.onclick=()=>{step--;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!.onclick=()=>{step++;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.onclick=()=>{step=0;render();};render();});
</script>
